=== Exercise 1: Zero-crossing failure with strong 2nd harmonic ===
  Fundamental period T0 = 8.33 ms
  Observation window T_obs = 50.0 ms -> 6.0 periods
  Roots in one period (rad): 0, 2.2459, 3.1416, 4.0373 -> 4 crossings/period
  Total zero crossings in 0.05s: 24
  Estimated frequency: 240.0 Hz (double the true F0 = 120 Hz!)

=== Exercise 2: FFT resolution and cent error ===
  FFT bin spacing df = 16000 / 640 = 25.0 Hz
  True frequency: 162.5 Hz, midway between bin 6 (150.0 Hz) and bin 7 (175.0 Hz)
  Max frequency error: 12.5 Hz
  Cent error vs bin 7: 128.30 cents
  Cent error vs bin 6: 138.57 cents

=== Exercise 3: Window normalization on small vector ===
  xw = [0.5 2.  6.  6.  2.  0.5]
  R_xw(0) = 80.500, R_xw(2) = 30.000
  R_w(0) = 2.6250, R_w(2) = 1.5000
  r_unnorm(2) = 0.3727
  r_norm(2) = 0.6522

=== Exercise 4: Metrics (VDE, GPE, FFE, cents) ===
  Total frames: 6
  VDE frames: [1, 2] -> VDE = 2/6 = 33.33%
  Both voiced frames: [0, 3, 4]
  GPE frames: [3] -> GPE = 1/3 = 33.33%
  FFE frames: [1, 2, 3] -> FFE = 3/6 = 50.00%
    Frame 1: +14.37 cents
    Frame 5: +38.91 cents
  Mean absolute fine cents: 26.64 cents

=== Exercise 5: Cycle budget and RTF at 25 MHz and 100 MHz ===
  At 25 MHz:
    Budget per 10 ms hop = 250000 cycles
    RTF_mac = 98543/250000 = 0.3942
    RTF_core = 99700/250000 = 0.3988
  At 100 MHz:
    Budget per 10 ms hop = 1000000 cycles
    RTF_mac = 98543/1000000 = 0.0985
    RTF_core = 99700/1000000 = 0.0997
  8-channel multiplexing total cycles per 10 ms = 797600
  Minimum clock frequency = 79.76 MHz
